# Template for the Pi's crontab. Compare it against what is actually
# installed with `crontab -l` before replacing anything, because the real
# schedule has only ever lived on the Pi.
#
# Install with `crontab crontab.example`, or paste into `crontab -e`.

# Take a reading on the hour and append it to the local buffer.
#
# check_temp.py writes exactly one line of JSON to stdout, which is what
# makes the append safe. Keep stderr pointed somewhere else: a traceback
# landing in the buffer would be an unreadable line that the upload has to
# skip.
#
# tee fans that same line out to a second, independent buffer for the new
# app's ingest API, alongside the MySQL one. Neither write path touches the
# other's buffer file.
#
# Without pipefail, cron would only ever see tee's exit status, so a crash
# in check_temp.py (still logged to check_temp.log via its own redirect)
# would be reported as success. bash -c with pipefail set makes a failure
# anywhere in the pipe, including tee itself failing to write a buffer,
# show up as a failed run. tee's own stderr is captured separately, since
# it is not one of the two redirects inside the quoted pipeline.
0 * * * * cd /home/pi && bash -c 'set -o pipefail; /usr/bin/python3 check_temp.py 2>> check_temp.log | /usr/bin/tee -a apartment_data_buffer.json >> apartment_data_buffer.api_buffer.json' 2>> tee.log

# Upload whatever has been buffered, a few minutes behind the reading so
# the two never overlap. Rows left over from a run with no network are
# picked up by the next one.
#
# flock keeps two uploads from running at once. A run that hangs on the
# database would otherwise still be holding the buffer when the next hour
# starts it again, and both would insert the same rows.
5 * * * * cd /home/pi && /usr/bin/flock -n /home/pi/upload.lock /usr/bin/python3 write_temp_to_db.py 2>> upload.log

# Send the same readings to the new temperature app's ingest API, during the
# parallel-rollout period. Fully independent of the MySQL upload above: its
# own buffer, its own lock, so the same offset is fine.
5 * * * * cd /home/pi && /usr/bin/flock -n /home/pi/api_upload.lock /usr/bin/python3 write_temp_to_api.py 2>> api_upload.log

# Listen for the joystick.
@reboot cd /home/pi && /usr/bin/python3 joystick_handler.py 2>> joystick.log
